---
system: sys-12-support-admin-operations
flow_id: login-and-mfa
surface: admin
spec_anchor: /software/systems/12-support-admin-operations#post-adminauthlogin
actors: [AdminConsole, AdminAuthService, PostgreSQL, AuditLog]
apis:
  - POST /admin/auth/login
  - POST /admin/auth/mfa-verify
  - POST /admin/auth/logout
externals: []
queues: []
failure_paths:
  - invalid_credentials
  - admin_login_rate_limited
  - account_disabled
  - mfa_token_invalid
  - mfa_totp_invalid
  - session_expired
idempotency: per-attempt audit log row; no idempotency key (auth flow is intentionally state-changing)
retry: caller-side no auto-retry on 401; 5 attempts per email per 10 min rate limit
timeout: 5s p99 per request
status: final
---
%% HAND-CURATED. mfa_required gated by admin_users.mfa_enabled (super_admin = required).
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant AdminConsole
    participant AdminAuthService
    participant PostgreSQL
    participant AuditLog

    AdminConsole->>AdminAuthService: POST /admin/auth/login {email, password}
    AdminAuthService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT COUNT login_attempt audit rows in last 10 min for email

    alt admin_login_rate_limited
        PostgreSQL-->>AdminAuthService: >= 5
        AdminAuthService-->>AdminConsole: 429 admin_login_rate_limited
    else under limit
        AdminAuthService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT id, password_hash, role, mfa_enabled, mfa_secret, status FROM admin_users WHERE email=$1
        alt invalid_credentials
            Note over AdminAuthService: email not found OR password_hash mismatch
            AdminAuthService->>AuditLog: append login_attempt {result: invalid_credentials}
            AdminAuthService-->>AdminConsole: 401 invalid_credentials
        else account_disabled
            PostgreSQL-->>AdminAuthService: row {status: disabled}
            AdminAuthService->>AuditLog: append login_attempt {result: account_disabled}
            AdminAuthService-->>AdminConsole: 403 account_disabled
        else mfa_required
            PostgreSQL-->>AdminAuthService: row {mfa_enabled: true}
            AdminAuthService->>AuditLog: append login_attempt {result: mfa_challenge_issued}
            AdminAuthService-->>AdminConsole: 200 {mfaRequired: true, mfaToken (short-lived JWT, purpose=mfa_challenge)}
            AdminConsole->>AdminAuthService: POST /admin/auth/mfa-verify {mfaToken, totp_code}
            alt mfa_token_invalid
                AdminAuthService-->>AdminConsole: 401 mfa_token_invalid (expired or wrong purpose)
            else mfa_totp_invalid
                AdminAuthService->>AuditLog: append mfa_verify {result: totp_invalid}
                AdminAuthService-->>AdminConsole: 401 mfa_totp_invalid
            else mfa_ok
                AdminAuthService->>PostgreSQL: INSERT admin_sessions (id, admin_user_id, expires_at)
                AdminAuthService->>AuditLog: append mfa_verify {result: success}
                AdminAuthService-->>AdminConsole: 200 {access_token, refresh_token}
            end
        else no_mfa_success
            PostgreSQL-->>AdminAuthService: row {mfa_enabled: false}
            AdminAuthService->>PostgreSQL: INSERT admin_sessions (id, admin_user_id, expires_at)
            AdminAuthService->>AuditLog: append login {result: success}
            AdminAuthService-->>AdminConsole: 200 {access_token, refresh_token}
        end
    end

    opt later logout
        AdminConsole->>AdminAuthService: POST /admin/auth/logout
        AdminAuthService->>PostgreSQL: DELETE admin_sessions WHERE id=$1
        AdminAuthService->>AuditLog: append logout
        AdminAuthService-->>AdminConsole: 204
    end

    Note over AdminConsole,AuditLog: every attempt audited regardless of result — MFA required for super_admin — session_expired returns 401 forcing re-login
